From bbf784926d9d37908b21a89dc8128a5f1c51e65f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 12:17:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ram: -write_select mask, a write port's words named by a mask
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A write port named the word it writes by an address, decoded per word.
A register file whose writes land on many words at once (one arriving
value written to every entry whose tag matched) had no port for it:
the array had to be flops and muxes outside the generator.

-write_select mask makes each write port's input a mask with a bit a
word, wsel (or wsel0, wsel1, ...) in place of addr_w. A word's select
is its bit, through the word's select buffer, with no decoder or
address inverters, so one write writes every word whose bit is set.
we still enables the write, and where ports write the same word in a
cycle -write_priority applies as for decoded writes. The behavioral
model writes by the mask too.

It needs the per-word selects of -decoder word or -banks, and write
ports only: a read/write port's address is also read (RAM-0129).
generate_array takes select=mask on its write ports, all of them alike
(RAM-0130).

Not upstreamed: on generate_array and the per-word decoder, carried
with them. Retires at a //:bump onto an OpenROAD that carries it.

Signed-off-by: Øyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
